    "body": "\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nFixes an issue where `LMCACHE_FORCE_SKIP_SAVE` evaluates to `True` even when explicitly set to `\"False\"` or `\"0\"`. Replaces improper `bool(...)` casting with an explicit truthy string check.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Fixes environment variable parsing bug where disabling `LMCACHE_FORCE_SKIP_SAVE` (e.g., `LMCACHE_FORCE_SKIP_SAVE=0` or `LMCACHE_FORCE_SKIP_SAVE=False`) was ignored.\r\n- Correctly parses `\"1\"`, `\"true\"`, and `\"yes\"` as `True`, and all other values (including unset or empty) as `False`.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nVerified via Python interactive session:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport os\r\n\r\ndef check(val):\r\n    if val is not None:\r\n        os.environ[\"LMCACHE_FORCE_SKIP_SAVE\"] = val\r\n    else:\r\n        os.environ.pop(\"LMCACHE_FORCE_SKIP_SAVE\", None)\r\n    return os.getenv(\"LMCACHE_FORCE_SKIP_SAVE\", \"\").lower() in (\"1\", \"true\", \"yes\")\r\n\r\n# Validations:\r\nassert check(\"False\") is False\r\nassert check(\"false\") is False\r\nassert check(\"0\") is False\r\nassert check(\"no\") is False\r\nassert check(\"\") is False\r\nassert check(None) is False\r\n\r\nassert check(\"1\") is True\r\nassert check(\"true\") is True\r\nassert check(\"True\") is True\r\nassert check(\"yes\") is True",
    "changed_files": 1,
